  (89, 'Comfrey', 'Symphytum officinale', 'Root', 'Allantoin', 'Nitrogenous compound', 'Ureide', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal contributor to cell proliferation, tissue repair, and wound healing.', 'I chose to profile the root because it is the medicinal part most consistently emphasized in the major monographs and contains the highest concentration of allantoin. The leaves have a somewhat different phytochemical profile (including generally lower allantoin and pyrrolizidine alkaloid levels).'),
