  (100, 'Coriander', 'Coriandrum sativum', 'Fruit (seed)', 'Linalool', 'Terpenoid', 'Monoterpenoid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal constituent responsible for carminative, digestive, antimicrobial, and mild anxiolytic activity.', 'I chose to profile the fruit (seed) rather than the leaf because it is the medicinal part represented in the major herbal monographs and has a chemistry dominated by linalool-rich volatile oil. The leaves ("cilantro") have a substantially different constituent profile and would warrant a separate entry if they were ever included in the database.'),
