  (95, 'Corn Silk', 'Zea mays', 'Stigma (silk)', 'Maysin', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavone glycoside', 'High', 'Marker', 'Characteristic flavone glycoside contributing antioxidant activity and serving as the principal phytochemical marker.', 'I chose maysin as the marker because it is the most characteristic flavonoid consistently associated with corn silk in modern phytochemical references. Earlier herbal texts often emphasize the mucilage and mineral content, but under your editorial rules we exclude minerals unless they define the herb. This profile therefore captures the principal chemically defined constituents while preserving the herb''s well-known demulcent and urinary-support actions.'),
