  (93, 'Cramp Bark', 'Viburnum opulus', 'Bark', 'Procyanidins', 'Tannin', 'Condensed tannin', 'Moderate', 'Present', 'Contribute antioxidant and mild astringent activity while supporting vascular tissues.', NULL),
  (52, 'Cranesbill', 'Geranium maculatum', 'Rhizome', 'Geraniin', 'Tannin', 'Ellagitannin', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal astringent constituent responsible for the herb''s tissue-toning, antidiarrheal, and hemostatic activity.', 'Cranesbill is a good example of a herb whose medicinal activity is dominated by its ellagitannins rather than by a diverse array of phytochemicals. I included geraniin and corilagin because they are consistently recognized as the principal hydrolyzable tannins in authoritative references. The remaining constituents help characterize the accompanying phenolic profile without diluting the herb''s primary identity as one of Western herbalism''s classic astringents.'),
  (52, 'Cranesbill', 'Geranium maculatum', 'Rhizome', 'Corilagin', 'Tannin', 'Ellagitannin', 'High', 'Major', 'Major ellagitannin contributing astringent, antioxidant, and anti-inflammatory activity.', NULL),
