  (84, 'Chamomile', 'Matricaria recutita', 'Flower', 'α-Bisabolol', 'Terpenoid', 'Monoterpenoid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Major contributor to anti-inflammatory, wound-healing, and gastroprotective activity.', 'α-Bisabolol and chamazulene are the two principal analytical markers of German chamomile and account for much of its anti-inflammatory reputation.
