  (99, 'Myrrh', 'Commiphora myrrha (C. molmol)', 'Oleo-gum-resin', 'Furanoeudesma-1,3-diene', 'Terpenoid', 'Sesquiterpene', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal sesquiterpene contributing anti-inflammatory, antimicrobial, and oral mucosal protective activity.', 'Myrrh is one of the few medicinal resins whose activity is distributed across volatile sesquiterpenes, non-volatile resin acids, and gum polysaccharides. Following the style guide, the profile avoids using "resin" or "oleoresin" as constituents and instead represents the major chemically defined components that together account for the herb''s medicinal properties.'),
