  (99, 'Myrrh', 'Commiphora myrrha (C. molmol)', 'Oleo-gum-resin', 'Acidic arabinogalactan-protein', 'Protein', 'Glycoprotein', 'Low–Moderate', 'Present', 'Contributes immunomodulatory activity as part of the gum fraction characteristic of myrrh.', NULL),
  (189, 'Nasturtium', 'Tropaeolum majus', 'Aerial parts', 'Glucotropaeolin', 'Glycoside', 'Glucosinolate', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal glucosinolate serving as the precursor to benzyl isothiocyanate and contributing antimicrobial activity.', 'Nasturtium is one of the few medicinal herbs outside the mustard seeds and horseradish in which the glucosinolate–isothiocyanate system is the defining medicinal chemistry. Unlike mustard, however, the medicinal material is the fresh aerial parts, making its phytochemical profile particularly useful for comparison with other Brassicales herbs used as urinary antiseptics.'),
  (189, 'Nasturtium', 'Tropaeolum majus', 'Aerial parts', 'Benzyl isothiocyanate', 'Organosulfur compound', 'Isothiocyanate', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal hydrolysis product responsible for antimicrobial and urinary antiseptic activity.', NULL),
