  (3, 'Japanese Angelica Tree', 'Aralia elata', 'Root bark', 'Elatoside A', 'Glycoside', 'Triterpenoid saponin', 'High', 'Marker', 'Characteristic oleanane saponin contributing to the herb''s adaptogenic and immunomodulatory activity.', 'Aralia elata is defined primarily by its oleanane triterpenoid saponins, especially the elatosides, which account for much of its adaptogenic, immunomodulatory, and anti-inflammatory activity. Because these saponins distinguish the species chemically, the profile emphasizes them over more widely distributed supporting phenolics or flavonoids.'),
  (3, 'Japanese Angelica Tree', 'Aralia elata', 'Root bark', 'Elatoside C', 'Glycoside', 'Triterpenoid saponin', 'High', 'Major', 'Major triterpenoid saponin representative of the characteristic elatoside fraction.', NULL),
