  (450, 'Khella', 'Ammi visnaga', 'Fruit', 'Khellin', 'Benzopyrone', 'Furanochromone', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal furanochromone contributing to the herb''s smooth muscle relaxant and bronchodilatory activity.', 'Ammi visnaga is defined primarily by its furanochromones, especially khellin and visnagin, which account for much of its smooth muscle relaxant, bronchodilatory, and vasodilatory activity. The accompanying pyranocoumarins complement this distinctive chemistry while remaining secondary to the defining furanochromone fraction.'),
