  (615, 'Kola', 'Cola nitida', 'Seed', 'Caffeine', 'Alkaloid', 'Purine alkaloid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal methylxanthine responsible for the herb''s central nervous system stimulant activity.', 'Cola nitida is defined primarily by its methylxanthine alkaloids, especially caffeine and theobromine, which account for much of its stimulant and cardiotonic activity. Flavan-3-ols and procyanidins provide the characteristic astringent polyphenol fraction but remain secondary to the dominant purine alkaloid chemistry.'),
