  (150, 'Kola Nut', 'Cola acuminata', 'Seed', 'Caffeine', 'Alkaloid', 'Purine alkaloid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal methylxanthine responsible for the herb''s stimulant and cognitive effects.', 'Cola acuminata is defined primarily by its methylxanthine alkaloids, especially caffeine and theobromine, which account for much of its stimulant and cardiotonic activity. The flavan-3-ols and procyanidins form a complementary astringent tannin fraction but remain secondary to the dominant purine alkaloid chemistry.'),
