  (14, 'Korean Ginseng', 'Panax ginseng', 'Root', 'Ginsenoside Rb1', 'Glycoside', 'Triterpenoid saponin', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal protopanaxadiol ginsenoside contributing to adaptogenic and immunomodulatory activity.', 'Panax ginseng is defined almost entirely by its ginsenosides, which account for much of its adaptogenic, immunomodulatory, neuroprotective, and metabolic activity. The inclusion of ginsenoside Rf highlights a constituent largely unique to Asian ginseng, reinforcing the characteristic chemistry that distinguishes Korean ginseng from its American counterpart.'),
