  (227, 'Kutki', 'Picrorhiza kurroa', 'Rhizome', 'Picroside I', 'Glycoside', 'Iridoid glycoside', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal iridoid glycoside contributing to the herb''s hepatoprotective and bitter tonic activity.', 'Picrorhiza kurroa is defined primarily by its intensely bitter iridoid glycosides, especially the picrosides and kutkoside, which account for much of its hepatoprotective, cholagogue, and digestive tonic activity. Supporting phenolics complement this chemistry, but the iridoid fraction remains the herb''s defining phytochemical feature.'),
  (227, 'Kutki', 'Picrorhiza kurroa', 'Rhizome', 'Picroside II', 'Glycoside', 'Iridoid glycoside', 'High', 'Marker', 'Characteristic iridoid glycoside widely used for quality control and liver-supportive activity.', NULL),
