  (535, 'Lemon', 'Citrus limon', 'Peel', 'Limonene', 'Terpenoid', 'Monoterpenoid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal volatile constituent responsible for much of the peel''s digestive and carminative activity.', 'Citrus limon peel is defined by abundant monoterpenes, particularly limonene, together with characteristic citrus flavanones that contribute digestive, antioxidant, and vascular-supporting activity. This profile emphasizes the peel''s distinctive volatile and flavonoid chemistry rather than the fruit''s vitamin C, which is nutritionally important but not chemotaxonomically distinctive.'),
