  (980, 'Lomatium', 'Lomatium dissectum', 'Root', 'Psoralen', 'Coumarin', 'Furanocoumarin', 'High', 'Marker', 'Characteristic linear furanocoumarin contributing to the herb''s antimicrobial and photobiological activity.', 'Lomatium dissectum is defined primarily by its furanocoumarins, which account for much of its traditional antimicrobial and antiviral reputation. Because these compounds overwhelmingly distinguish the genus chemically, the profile emphasizes representative furanocoumarins rather than introducing common supporting flavonoids or terpenoids.'),
