  (448, 'Ma Huang', 'Ephedra sinica', 'Stem', 'Methylpseudoephedrine', 'Alkaloid', 'Phenethylamine alkaloid', 'Low–Moderate', 'Present', 'Representative minor ephedra alkaloid completing the defining alkaloid fraction.', NULL),
  (4, 'Manchurian Aralia', 'Aralia mandshurica', 'Root bark', 'Araloside A', 'Glycoside', 'Triterpenoid saponin', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal oleanane saponin contributing to the herb''s adaptogenic and immunomodulatory activity.', 'Aralia mandshurica is defined primarily by its araloside triterpenoid saponins, which account for much of its adaptogenic, immunomodulatory, and anti-inflammatory activity. Because these saponins overwhelmingly distinguish the species chemically, the profile emphasizes them over more ubiquitous supporting phenolics or flavonoids.'),
