  (4, 'Manchurian Aralia', 'Aralia mandshurica', 'Root bark', 'Hederagenin', 'Terpenoid', 'Oleanane triterpenoid', 'Moderate', 'Present', 'Characteristic sapogenin supporting the herb''s triterpenoid profile.', NULL),
  (1253, 'Manzanita', 'Arctostaphylos manzanita', 'Leaf', 'Arbutin', 'Glycoside', 'Phenolic glycoside', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal phenolic glycoside contributing to the herb''s traditional urinary antiseptic activity.', 'Arctostaphylos manzanita is defined primarily by its hydroquinone glycosides, especially arbutin, which account for much of its urinary antiseptic and astringent activity. Hydrolyzable tannins reinforce these actions, while flavonoids provide secondary antioxidant support without defining the species'' characteristic chemistry.'),
