  (NULL, 'Maral Root', 'Rhaponticum carthamoides', 'Root', '20-Hydroxyecdysone', 'Steroid', 'Phytoecdysteroid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal phytoecdysteroid associated with the herb''s adaptogenic and anabolic reputation.', 'Rhaponticum carthamoides is defined primarily by its phytoecdysteroids, especially 20-hydroxyecdysone, which account for much of its adaptogenic, anabolic, and exercise-supportive reputation. The inclusion of rhaponticin represents the herb''s distinctive stilbene chemistry while preserving the dominant ecdysteroid profile.'),
