  (107, 'Marjoram', 'Origanum majorana', 'Aerial parts', 'Terpinen-4-ol', 'Terpenoid', 'Monoterpenoid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal monoterpene alcohol contributing antimicrobial and aromatic activity.', 'Origanum majorana is defined primarily by oxygenated monoterpenes, especially terpinen-4-ol and cis-sabinene hydrate, which account for much of its aromatic, antimicrobial, digestive, and mild antispasmodic activity. Rosmarinic acid provides complementary antioxidant activity while remaining secondary to the herb''s distinctive volatile chemistry.'),
