  (87, 'Willow', 'Salix spp.', 'Bark', 'Salicin', 'Glycoside', 'Phenolic glycoside', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal phenolic glycoside responsible for much of the bark''s analgesic, antipyretic, and anti-inflammatory activity.', 'Salix bark is chemically defined by its salicylate glycosides, which account for much of its traditional analgesic, antipyretic, and anti-inflammatory activity. Flavan-3-ols and condensed tannins provide complementary antioxidant and astringent effects while remaining secondary to the characteristic salicylate chemistry that distinguishes the genus.'),
  (87, 'Willow', 'Salix spp.', 'Bark', 'Salicortin', 'Glycoside', 'Phenolic glycoside', 'High', 'Major', 'Characteristic salicylate glycoside supporting the defining analgesic chemistry.', NULL),
