  (645, 'Yellow Jasmine', 'Gelsemium sempervirens', 'Root', 'Koumine', 'Alkaloid', 'Indole alkaloid', 'Moderate', 'Present', 'Well-documented indole alkaloid complementing the characteristic Gelsemium alkaloid profile.', NULL),
  (645, 'Yellow Jasmine', 'Gelsemium sempervirens', 'Root', 'Gelsedine', 'Alkaloid', 'Indole alkaloid', 'Low–Moderate', 'Present', 'Representative indole alkaloid complementing the characteristic Gelsemium alkaloid profile.', NULL),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', 'Caffeine', 'Alkaloid', 'Purine alkaloid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal methylxanthine responsible for much of the herb''s stimulant and cognitive effects.', 'Ilex paraguariensis is chemically defined by its methylxanthines together with its abundant caffeoylquinic acids, which account for much of its stimulant, antioxidant, and metabolic activity. The flavonoids provide a complementary phenolic fraction while preserving the dominant caffeine–chlorogenic acid chemistry that distinguishes yerba mate.'),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', 'Theobromine', 'Alkaloid', 'Purine alkaloid', 'High', 'Major', 'Characteristic methylxanthine contributing complementary stimulant and vasodilatory activity.', NULL),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', 'Chlorogenic acid', 'Polyphenol', 'Caffeoylquinic acid', 'High', 'Major', 'Principal hydroxycinnamate contributing antioxidant activity and defining the major phenolic fraction.', NULL),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', '3,5-Dicaffeoylquinic acid', 'Polyphenol', 'Caffeoylquinic acid', 'Moderate', 'Major', 'Representative dicaffeoylquinic acid reinforcing the characteristic chlorogenic acid complex.', NULL),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', 'Rutin', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavonol glycoside', 'Moderate', 'Present', 'Characteristic flavonoid complementing the dominant methylxanthine and caffeoylquinic acid chemistry.', NULL),
  (617, 'Yerba Mate', 'Ilex paraguariensis', 'Leaf', 'Caffeic acid', 'Polyphenol', 'Hydroxycinnamic acid', 'Low–Moderate', 'Present', 'Representative hydroxycinnamic acid complementing the abundant caffeoylquinic acid fraction.', NULL),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Eriodictyol', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavanone', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal flavanone contributing to the herb''s characteristic respiratory, antioxidant, and anti-inflammatory activity.', 'Eriodictyon californicum is chemically defined by its flavanones, particularly eriodictyol, homoeriodictyol, sterubin, and related compounds, which account for much of its traditional respiratory activity and modern neuroprotective interest. The profile intentionally emphasizes this highly characteristic flavanone chemistry before introducing minor supporting flavones, preserving the constituent family that distinguishes the genus.'),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Homoeriodictyol', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavanone', 'High', 'Major', 'Characteristic flavanone responsible for the herb''s well-known taste-modifying and bitter-masking properties.', NULL),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Sterubin', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavanone', 'High', 'Major', 'Characteristic flavanone increasingly recognized as a major neuroprotective and anti-inflammatory constituent.', NULL),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Sakuranetin', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavanone', 'Moderate', 'Major', 'Representative flavanone reinforcing the defining flavanone chemistry of the genus.', NULL),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Genkwanin', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavone', 'Moderate', 'Present', 'Methylated flavone complementing the dominant flavanone profile.', NULL),
  (590, 'Yerba Santa', 'Eriodictyon californicum', 'Leaf', 'Chrysoeriol', 'Flavonoid', 'Flavone', 'Low–Moderate', 'Present', 'Methylated flavone complementing the dominant flavanone fraction and characteristic flavonoid profile.', NULL),
  (745, 'Ylang Ylang', 'Cananga odorata', 'Flower', 'Linalool', 'Terpenoid', 'Monoterpenoid', 'High', 'Marker', 'Principal monoterpene alcohol contributing to the flower''s characteristic floral aroma and calming activity.', 'Cananga odorata is chemically defined by its complex floral volatile chemistry, particularly its monoterpene alcohols, sesquiterpenes, and aromatic esters, which account for much of its traditional calming effects and its importance in perfumery. The profile emphasizes the compounds that distinguish ylang ylang''s characteristic fragrance while avoiding less diagnostic minor constituents.'),
  (745, 'Ylang Ylang', 'Cananga odorata', 'Flower', 'Germacrene D', 'Terpenoid', 'Sesquiterpene', 'High', 'Major', 'Characteristic sesquiterpene contributing substantially to the essential oil profile.', NULL),
  (745, 'Ylang Ylang', 'Cananga odorata', 'Flower', 'β-Caryophyllene', 'Terpenoid', 'Sesquiterpene', 'Moderate', 'Major', 'Representative sesquiterpene supporting the anti-inflammatory and aromatic properties of the oil.', NULL),
  (745, 'Ylang Ylang', 'Cananga odorata', 'Flower', 'Benzyl benzoate', 'Phenylpropanoid', 'Benzoate ester', 'Moderate', 'Major', 'Characteristic aromatic ester contributing to the fragrance profile and traditional topical applications.', NULL),
